# [BUG] Shared key is exposed when msg or seed come from keyvault

- Source URL: https://github.com/chipsalliance/adams-bridge/issues/227

The shared key can be read over the API if the msg or seed come from the keyvault, but the shared key was not programmed to write to the keyvault.

The data present bits are being reset as soon as the valids are asserted, which allows the shared key api to be read out.

The fix is to only reset the data present bits on the mandatory zeroize.

PR Title: [RTL] Fix bug 227, only reset kv data present bits on mandatory zeroize

Description:
The pull request addresses a security vulnerability in Caliptra's instantiation of the adams-bridge component. The issue involved keyvault data present bits, which are designed to protect shared keys from being read when source data originates from the keyvault. Previously, these protection bits were being reset at the end of operations, potentially exposing the shared key through the read API if the destination wasn't set to the keyvault.

The fix ensures that "data present bits will be reset when the mandatory zeroize is issued between operations."

